      "kind": "finding",
      "title": "Earth screening tests and microgravity can disagree",
      "text": "In SAFFIRE-II, 4 of 4 silicone sheets showed about 0 cm of burning in microgravity at 20 cm/s airflow, yet 2 of them burned completely in the matching normal-gravity tests. The cotton-fiberglass sheet (2-5) burned its full 29 cm in microgravity.",
      "so_what": "Material screening done on Earth does not map one-to-one onto flammability in a spacecraft; the direction of the difference depends on the material.",
      "caveat": "9 samples; O2 about 21.5-22.1% (derived by NASA from CO2 production).",
